What was taken
--------------
The 'sales' and 'finance' divisions only (14 files). The upstream repository
carries 230+ agents across ~20 divisions; the rest — engineering, game
development, GIS, healthcare — have no bearing on a GCC Odoo consultancy and
were deliberately left behind.

Why vendored rather than fetched
--------------------------------
These files shape what C2P's agents say to real prospects. Pinning them to a
commit means a change upstream cannot alter our outreach without a reviewed
diff landing in this repository first. Same discipline as c2p_agents: content
that decides behaviour belongs in version control, not fetched at run time.

How to update
-------------
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/msitarzewski/agency-agents /tmp/aa
  cp /tmp/aa/sales/*.md   delivery_api/data/agent_library/sales/
  cp /tmp/aa/finance/*.md delivery_api/data/agent_library/finance/
  # then update Commit/Retrieved above and review the diff before committing

These files are upstream's work, unmodified. Local adaptation belongs in
agent_library.py, which reads them, so that a refresh stays a clean copy.
